{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions","id":561655,"title":"Sardonyx questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-20T00:35:15-07:00","id":561655,"title":"Sardonyx questions","content":"As I got a general question and the topics so far didn't really lend themselves to ppl posting such things into them (the general sardonix thread still is more about comments,... than questions and answers thus then this thread). So if anyone has questions about things that seem confusing,... you are freee to also post in here.<br /> <br /> So now to my own question. I've read through all three teasers and sardonix seems quite complete there and mostly easy to understand (if you think it through) BUT what really confuses me is the initiative system. Am I understanding it correctly that when the first player acts then afterwards (in order of taht the first player declares who is the second one to act and the second who is the third one to act, ...) all players act immediately? Or are the players still acting on the ticks that were rolled (only that the order of WHICH player acts on WHICH tick is chosen by them there)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T12:56:54-07:00","id":562159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions#post561655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I got a general question and the topics so far didn't really lend themselves to ppl posting such things into them (the general sardonix thread still is more about comments,... than questions and answers thus then this thread). So if anyone has questions about things that seem confusing,... you are freee to also post in here.<br /> <br /> So now to my own question. I've read through all three teasers and sardonix seems quite complete there and mostly easy to understand (if you think it through) BUT what really confuses me is the initiative system. Am I understanding it correctly that when the first player acts then afterwards (in order of taht the first player declares who is the second one to act and the second who is the third one to act, ...) all players act immediately? Or are the players still acting on the ticks that were rolled (only that the order of WHICH player acts on WHICH tick is chosen by them there)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if they got rid of the Tick Wheel or not, so that might make a difference. The differences in starting ticks is probably not great though, with the more limited dice pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T15:34:09-07:00","id":562278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=562159#post562159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if they got rid of the Tick Wheel or not, so that might make a difference. The differences in starting ticks is probably not great though, with the more limited dice pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just throwing my hat in the ring, this is neither an advantage or disadvantage, but the party scholar at least won't have to wait for the warrior to act three times before they get a turn. I believe that ticks are going to remain as is, which is a shame because I prefer rounds with multiple initiative segments (segment one everybody acts, segment two those with speed 2+ act, and so on until segment X where you've hit the speed cap) so that slow characters are involved right from the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T17:30:29-07:00","id":562383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=562159#post562159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if they got rid of the Tick Wheel or not, so that might make a difference. The differences in starting ticks is probably not great though, with the more limited dice pools.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is no Tick Wheel. That's an Exalted 2e thing. The only similarity between the two is the use of the word &quot;tick.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T08:07:32-07:00","id":563029,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it works like this:<br /> <br /> Everybody rolls for initiative. Director rolls for director characters/groups.<br /> <br /> If the highest roll is a director character, that character goes first. If the highest roll is a player, that character goes first.<br /> <br /> Then it alternates between player and director. So it would be Player 1 -&gt; Director Character -&gt; Player 2 -&gt; Director Character and so on. If the players are all done before all the director characters are finished, the remaining director characters go. If all the director characters have gone, then all the players get a go.<br /> <br /> Players determine order by just saying who is next. The first person is whoever rolled highest, but after that it's who that player says, then the next person, etcetera. There is no tick wheel, no ticks, and no tick cost on actions. Tick order is completely irrelevant. You just kinda do your thing, if possible. So except for determining the first player, &quot;tick order&quot; is meaningless on the PC side.<br /> <br /> For director characters, they go in tick order/initiative order as rolled, from highest to lowest.<br /> <br /> When everyone is gone, you have a new round. The last player in the previous round is the first player to act (LIFO), and the first director character in the previous round is the first director character to act (FIFO). If the last person to act last round was a director character/group/side, then the players act first this round. If the last person to act last round was a player/the player side, then the director character acts first.<br /> <br /> That it. It's one roll, made at the start of the fight, and mostly matters for who goes very first, who starts with focus, and order of director character actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T08:09:17-07:00","id":563031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=562383#post562383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There is no Tick Wheel. That's an Exalted 2e thing. The only similarity between the two is the use of the word &quot;tick.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It really strikes me as better to drop the use of that word as being needlessly confusing. It's going to confuse people familiar with Exalted 2nd, and to a lesser extent Scion, and it doesn't really still make sense to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T10:01:56-07:00","id":563084,"title":"","content":"It's an open-dev extremely early system-engine document. As many of the devs have said, the names for many things are placeholders that aren't going to be in the final cuts of the actual games built on the engine once released.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry about &quot;tick&quot; being confusing. Either it will make sense in the total system despite doing something different (I can think of countless common terms in RPGs that mean different things in different games; even games linked with the same company) and stay, or a better term will come out of the full development process.<br /> <br /> It's way too early for us to know if Tick is a problem hold-over term or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T11:53:41-07:00","id":563216,"title":"","content":"Don't know how this became a tick / naming discussion though. The original question was: How is the initiative system supposed to really work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:15:38-07:00","id":563242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=563084#post563084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an open-dev extremely early system-engine document. As many of the devs have said, the names for many things are placeholders that aren't going to be in the final cuts of the actual games built on the engine once released.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really the <i>best</i> time to criticize any names or not, because they aren't finalized yet. We have no way of knowing what is a placeholder and what is not - it's not like they are highlighted in red or on some list we can readily compare to. So if we have an issue with the name of something now really is the best time to bring it up, before that name gets put on dozens of pages across multiple documents that will then need to be corrected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't worry about &quot;tick&quot; being confusing. Either it will make sense in the total system despite doing something different (I can think of countless common terms in RPGs that mean different things in different games; even games linked with the same company) and stay, or a better term will come out of the full development process.<br /> <br /> It's way too early for us to know if Tick is a problem hold-over term or not. </div> </div> </div>Except it quite obviously is, because see the OP. We already have someone needlessly confused by the name tick because of previous iterations of initiative systems using the word &quot;tick&quot;. Also <i>this is the development process we are doing right now</i>. This is how we get a better name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:17:17-07:00","id":563244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=563216#post563216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know how this became a tick / naming discussion though. The original question was: How is the initiative system supposed to really work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I explained that here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, it works like this:<br /> <br /> Everybody rolls for initiative. Director rolls for director characters/groups.<br /> <br /> If the highest roll is a director character, that character goes first. If the highest roll is a player, that character goes first.<br /> <br /> Then it alternates between player and director. So it would be Player 1 -&gt; Director Character -&gt; Player 2 -&gt; Director Character and so on. If the players are all done before all the director characters are finished, the remaining director characters go. If all the director characters have gone, then all the players get a go.<br /> <br /> Players determine order by just saying who is next. The first person is whoever rolled highest, but after that it's who that player says, then the next person, etcetera. There is no tick wheel, no ticks, and no tick cost on actions. Tick order is completely irrelevant. You just kinda do your thing, if possible. So except for determining the first player, &quot;tick order&quot; is meaningless on the PC side.<br /> <br /> For director characters, they go in tick order/initiative order as rolled, from highest to lowest.<br /> <br /> When everyone is gone, you have a new round. The last player in the previous round is the first player to act (LIFO), and the first director character in the previous round is the first director character to act (FIFO). If the last person to act last round was a director character/group/side, then the players act first this round. If the last person to act last round was a player/the player side, then the director character acts first.<br /> <br /> That it. It's one roll, made at the start of the fight, and mostly matters for who goes very first, who starts with focus, and order of director character actions. </div> </div> </div>Can you tell me what is still confusing you? I'll try to help more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T13:59:05-07:00","id":563390,"title":"","content":"tbh I overlooked your post before^^' (the tick posts had my concentration there). Ok then it is as I had hoped it was but wasn't sure from the formulation (wasn't sure if I translated it correctly). <br /> I don't really care if its called tick oer not^^ the thing taht confused me was solely how it was formulated as I wasn't sure if I translated it correctly or not.<br /> <br /> Tnx! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:25:58-07:00","id":563602,"title":"","content":"Hmm. This system doesn't really lend itself to ambushes and seems to discard 'slow lumbering monsters' going last, because the other side <i>immediately</i> goes after the first your first person.<br /> <br /> Even worse, it doesn't seem to allow for multi-sided combats easily. I also don't see any system for 'joining' into the combat late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T19:52:21-07:00","id":563665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=563602#post563602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. This system doesn't really lend itself to ambushes and seems to discard 'slow lumbering monsters' going last, because the other side <i>immediately</i> goes after the first your first person.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know how ambushes work. It doesn't seem like it will be hard to have as most games do: if you successfully sneak up on people you get an action and then normal combat starts.<br /> <br /> Also, Director characters go in order. So the slow lumbering giant enemy is the last Director character to act. The players are the ones that get to buck that trend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even worse, it doesn't seem to allow for multi-sided combats easily. I also don't see any system for 'joining' into the combat late. </div> </div> </div>The game doesn't really seem oriented towards the PCs being on multiple sides. Though it seems easy enough:<br /> <br /> PC Group 1, PC Group 2, Director. Repeat.<br /> <br /> Joining combat doesn't really seem to be a problem. PCs come in and get picked when another player picks them. A new Director character rolls and gets slotted into the order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T22:39:41-07:00","id":563740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=563602#post563602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. This system doesn't really lend itself to ambushes and seems to discard 'slow lumbering monsters' going last, because the other side <i>immediately</i> goes after the first your first person.<br /> <br /> Even worse, it doesn't seem to allow for multi-sided combats easily. I also don't see any system for 'joining' into the combat late.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) You wouldn't see who acts first in an ambush because the ambushers are the only people aware that an action scene is starting. If they conceal their intentions, then initiative is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;Slow, lumbering monsters&quot; don't move as fast, so they're going to take time to get to you in any event.<br /> <br /> 3) In the rare event of multiple PC sides, the system is the same--the handoff just isn't cooperative. Yet everybody *does* get to go, and if you decide to make the other side wait to be last . . . they go first next time. You could split them into two groups and do separate handoffs if you like, but I think the former option is a more interesting strategic choice. WRT NPCs, the Director slots them in whether they're allied or not. As noted above, new combatants get picked or rolled in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T06:35:05-07:00","id":564049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=563665#post563665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't know how ambushes work. It doesn't seem like it will be hard to have as most games do: if you successfully sneak up on people you get an action and then normal combat starts.<br /> <br /> Also, Director characters go in order. So the slow lumbering giant enemy is the last Director character to act. The players are the ones that get to buck that trend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it doesn't need to be any more complex than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T06:46:44-07:00","id":564071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=563740#post563740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) &quot;Slow, lumbering monsters&quot; don't move as fast, so they're going to take time to get to you in any event.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet your 'zombies' that have the lowest initiative (even if they are on multiple sides) are still going to go right after the fastest initiative. It doesn't matter how slow they are in the least.<br /> <br /> You might as well flip heads or tails to see if the PCs or the NPCs go first. It could be Superman and the Flash vs. two slow super zombies. Somehow that zombie is still getting to go faster than two super-speedsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T07:32:06-07:00","id":564116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=564071#post564071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet your 'zombies' that have the lowest initiative (even if they are on multiple sides) are still going to go right after the fastest initiative. It doesn't matter how slow they are in the least.<br /> <br /> You might as well flip heads or tails to see if the PCs or the NPCs go first. It could be Superman and the Flash vs. two slow super zombies. Somehow that zombie is still getting to go faster than two super-speedsters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or, maybe, the Powers that the super-speedsters have will alter the initiative order. Or maybe zombies will have a disadvantage that forces them to only go after all other characters. Or maybe Sardonyx doesn't care about physical speed, and only reflects the &quot;camera's focus.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T09:01:03-07:00","id":564173,"title":"","content":"Considering that in combat everyone is going, more or less, at about the same time, the notion of &quot;camera's focus&quot; isn't really a bad one. The whole &quot;Us, them, us, them&quot; thing is more of a book keeping, out of character, means to narrate what is basically just a big pile on. Being fast guarantees, mechanically, that someone on your side (in RP terms it's probably you) is going to get in the first shot. But at that point it's basically an all in, with arms and legs and khopeshes swinginging this way and that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T10:10:52-07:00","id":564232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=564071#post564071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet your 'zombies' that have the lowest initiative (even if they are on multiple sides) are still going to go right after the fastest initiative. It doesn't matter how slow they are in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, zombies are going to be a group, and whichever PC goes first if we're talking Superman/Flash level characters vs. shambling zombies, easily dispatches them.<br /> <br /> The problem with hyperbolic examples is that sometimes they really undermine your point. In this case, the rules seem perfectly well designed to ensure this isn't a problem. Mostly because there's really no reason to be rolling this out in the first place. The game already had guidelines for not breaking out the dice, and Superman + the Flash vs. 2 Shamblers is not a time to break out the dice. And then beyond that, the system has rules to treat zombies as a group, and it's really just whichever of the superheroes squishes them first. And then beyond that, either Superman or the Flash is going to have Focus, so as an example, the Flash squishes zombie 1, and then Superman steals the scene by grabbing and squishing zombie 2 right before it can bite the Flash who got distracted pulling himself out of zombie guts.<br /> <br /> Even with the scant preview we have... there's just a mountain of layers clearly baked into the developer's concepts to make sure this sort of thing will only happen if the Director wants it to happen; not because of some sort of fluke mistake in the rules.<br /> <br /> As as PaulChapman said, on top of this there's still going to be powers that might be able to impact action order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T13:49:26-07:00","id":564510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=564071#post564071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet your 'zombies' that have the lowest initiative (even if they are on multiple sides) are still going to go right after the fastest initiative. It doesn't matter how slow they are in the least.<br /> <br /> You might as well flip heads or tails to see if the PCs or the NPCs go first. It could be Superman and the Flash vs. two slow super zombies. Somehow that zombie is still getting to go faster than two super-speedsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have ticks in there specifically for speed altering powers. We could have omitted the initial roll/tick generation completely, but we kept it to allow such plugins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T17:15:39-07:00","id":564769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=564116#post564116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Or, maybe, the Powers that the super-speedsters have will alter the initiative order. Or maybe zombies will have a disadvantage that forces them to only go after all other characters. Or maybe Sardonyx doesn't care about physical speed, and only reflects the &quot;camera's focus.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It removes a style of play of 'fast squishy characters that act/react faster than their enemies'.<br /> <br /> Take your two fastest squishy characters and a brick against one slow foe that has an area of effect attack.<br /> <br /> Your faster characters roll a high initiative, your brick is slow. And lastly you your slow foe who rolled lowest.<br /> <br /> Speedster A goes first and realized the danger of the slow foe with a damaging fire aura. He takes his action and retreats out of range. Slow aura burning monster goes, killing the second speedster, because he didn't get to go faster than the monster. The brick is a bit hurt, but finally gets to go, even though he was still a little faster.<br /> <br /> It <i>penalizes</i> faster characters by not allowing them to react with their faster speeds before the the slow danger can hit them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","user":"ArthurHansen","date":". 06-22-2015, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T18:50:05-07:00","id":564832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=564769#post564769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It <i>penalizes</i> faster characters by not allowing them to react with their faster speeds before the the slow danger can hit them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're going to ignore Malcolm's post that speedsters will have powers that allow them to alter the initiative order? <br /> <br /> This shouldn't come as a surprise, but for a game with super powers, you really need to see the powers before you declare anything broken. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T19:11:15-07:00","id":564841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=564769#post564769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It removes a style of play of 'fast squishy characters that act/react faster than their enemies'.<br /> <br /> Take your two fastest squishy characters and a brick against one slow foe that has an area of effect attack.<br /> <br /> Your faster characters roll a high initiative, your brick is slow. And lastly you your slow foe who rolled lowest.<br /> <br /> Speedster A goes first and realized the danger of the slow foe with a damaging fire aura. He takes his action and retreats out of range. Slow aura burning monster goes, killing the second speedster, because he didn't get to go faster than the monster. The brick is a bit hurt, but finally gets to go, even though he was still a little faster.<br /> <br /> It <i>penalizes</i> faster characters by not allowing them to react with their faster speeds before the the slow danger can hit them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, if the speedster goes first he has no way to know what the slow opponent will do. Speedster A goes, then the slow aura guy kills *him* because he can't react, then Speedster B has all resources available to evade the attack instead of blowing them in a prior action. So the true scenario is the *opposite*. And in fact, speed would be well-represented by the act of evading the enemy.<br /> <br /> Previous games compensated for this by having everyone declare in reverse initiative order, then go, but the overwhelming experience of most groups is that this step was either omitted out of haste or forgetfulness, or highly disliked for slowing down play.<br /> <br /> Initiative represents winning at acting first, but in most systems, *losing* at information acquisition. You go first without the benefit of being informed about subsequent actions. There are solutions, as above, but they're often clunky.<br /> <br /> The other funny thing about initiative? It was never ever realistic. Combat is a set of relationships between people and objects that has too many dimensions to really portray with a single trait set. We do it to simplify things, but to understand its inaccuracy, go it up an old fencing coach. After he or she stop hits (scores in such a way as to interrupt your attempt to score) you over and over again, and after you go faster and faster, you may realize that the coach has a superior sense of timing separate from his or her raw reaction time to general stimuli.<br /> <br /> Now put a gun in the coach's hands and pit him or her against a trick shooter, to see who hits the fastest. Fencing coach loses. Speed is often *activity-specific*. But we can't model that in a system where actions are assumed to be dynamic and complex, and we do have superhumans who *do* have a general quality of speed. <br /> <br /> Fortunately, we have other tools to represent the various forms of speed. We gave systems for movement and to evade attacks. Reducing speed to the question of the order people go in (especially given that nobody really gets to go first or last after the first round, since rounds simply divide narrative time into chunks) doesn't really do it justice. We can produce powers systems for speedsters, and after that, use these other systems and trust in player control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T17:19:36-07:00","id":565883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=564841#post564841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, if the speedster goes first he has no way to know what the slow opponent will do. Speedster A goes, then the slow aura guy kills *him* because he can't react, then Speedster B has all resources available to evade the attack instead of blowing them in a prior action. So the true scenario is the *opposite*. And in fact, speed would be well-represented by the act of evading the enemy.<br /> <br /> Previous games compensated for this by having everyone declare in reverse initiative order, then go, but the overwhelming experience of most groups is that this step was either omitted out of haste or forgetfulness, or highly disliked for slowing down play.<br /> <br /> Initiative represents winning at acting first, but in most systems, *losing* at information acquisition. You go first without the benefit of being informed about subsequent actions. There are solutions, as above, but they're often clunky.<br /> <br /> The other funny thing about initiative? It was never ever realistic. Combat is a set of relationships between people and objects that has too many dimensions to really portray with a single trait set. We do it to simplify things, but to understand its inaccuracy, go it up an old fencing coach. After he or she stop hits (scores in such a way as to interrupt your attempt to score) you over and over again, and after you go faster and faster, you may realize that the coach has a superior sense of timing separate from his or her raw reaction time to general stimuli.<br /> <br /> Now put a gun in the coach's hands and pit him or her against a trick shooter, to see who hits the fastest. Fencing coach loses. Speed is often *activity-specific*. But we can't model that in a system where actions are assumed to be dynamic and complex, and we do have superhumans who *do* have a general quality of speed.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, we have other tools to represent the various forms of speed. We gave systems for movement and to evade attacks. Reducing speed to the question of the order people go in (especially given that nobody really gets to go first or last after the first round, since rounds simply divide narrative time into chunks) doesn't really do it justice. We can produce powers systems for speedsters, and after that, use these other systems and trust in player control.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not totally true that the speedster has no idea at all what an opponent would likely do. It doesn't exactly take mind reading to know that being in melee with most giants is bad. But in the current system (even with people being able to jump initiative order) one of those speedsters isn't going to get to even think of taking the action of 'leave melee before I get splatted/burned/melted'.<br /> <br /> Even if Speedster B has a power he can use at any point, that allows him to jump ahead of Speedster A, now Speedster A is suddenly going slower than the huge obvious slow threat.<br /> <br /> I can't see any dramatic or narrative reason to let the opponent automatically go right after the fastest hero. That seems more rooted in 'let the badguy get in at least one shot, no matter how slow he is'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T17:29:33-07:00","id":565885,"title":"","content":"You're over thinking it, If they have a power that allows them to jump the cue it'll be similar to Focus, where it doesn't actually upset said cue.<br /> <br /> Player 1<br /> DC 1<br /> Player 2<br /> <br /> becomes<br /> <br /> Player 2 w/ power<br /> Player 1<br /> DC1<br /> <br /> Director Characters wouldn't be drafting off the speedster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T20:20:48-07:00","id":565991,"title":"","content":"That isn't how I read it, as I got the impression that it didn't matter who went fast, the other side's highest initiative then gets to go second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T20:32:50-07:00","id":565993,"title":"","content":"Basic Initiative, sure, but once powers kick in the rules change. that's how all the games work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T23:56:24-07:00","id":566149,"title":"","content":"Although, frankly, sometimes the fast guys get snotted. It happens. And if you'll recall the many threads with 'How do I cope with a fast guy in a party of slow guys' and What to do about Untouchable Opponent' that was a real problem in the original Scion; fast initiative uncatchable characters made it a nightmare for everyone else. <i>Something</i> has to be done about it. And in this model the bad guy may go before the fast guy but he still has to <i>catch</i> him.<br /> <br /> Yeah, area of effect damage is going to suck in that case but you'd hope that the squishable guys would have noticed it prior to it becoming a thing and already have declined to engage, or moved to avoid it. Otherwise it's little different to a Titan cultist exploding a hidden explosive vest in the middle of melee in the current game, or any other kind of surprise area of attack thing. It happens. Bad guys use tactics too and sometimes the fast guy gets caught in the same way that the lumbering (yet invincible) brick meets an opponent who he can't catch, wherein all his strength and durability become meaningless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T01:44:36-07:00","id":566195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=565883#post565883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not totally true that the speedster has no idea at all what an opponent would likely do. It doesn't exactly take mind reading to know that being in melee with most giants is bad. But in the current system (even with people being able to jump initiative order) one of those speedsters isn't going to get to even think of taking the action of 'leave melee before I get splatted/burned/melted'.<br /> <br /> Even if Speedster B has a power he can use at any point, that allows him to jump ahead of Speedster A, now Speedster A is suddenly going slower than the huge obvious slow threat.<br /> <br /> I can't see any dramatic or narrative reason to let the opponent automatically go right after the fastest hero. That seems more rooted in 'let the badguy get in at least one shot, no matter how slow he is'.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's already an action for not getting hit by a guy because you're fast. It's dodging. If you can't dodge the big guy then you ain't really that fast, are ya? Dodging represents speed *better* because the character evading attack has both the representation of getting out of the way (by dodging) *and* the information advantage of knowing which attack is coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 06-24-2015, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T08:23:08-07:00","id":566436,"title":"","content":"Arthur:<br /> <br /> I think you're trying to break a system without the whole thing in front of you. It comes off as a bit silly.<br /> <br /> Yes, there is a critical value in pushing the system to find out what its breaking points are. It isn't an inherently negative judgement because all games have them and it can be very useful to know where they are.<br /> <br /> At the same time, such efforts are only really valuable if you approach the system with good faith. For example:<br /> <br /> If the Director wants a ridiculously slow to act character with this initiative system... don't have him attack the first action he gets. Our giant is dimwitted and slow, and didn't realize a fight was breaking out around him. His first action is to grab his 2 ton club. Bam. All the PCs will get at least one action before he swings that baby at anyone.<br /> <br /> The Director (or ST or GM or whatever) needs to design enemies that actually act mechanically how they are described.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the initiative system, a character that is so slow and uses such and unwieldy weapon that they can only attack every other action, is going to <i>feel</i> a heck of a lot slower than a character that can attack every round. Who goes first in a round is far less meaningful than how much you can get done in one.<br /> <br /> If you want a super-low giant that feels slow, you have to make him actually slow; not just slot him at the end of init.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T15:15:28-07:00","id":567056,"title":"","content":"There is a possible solution in that genuinely slow characters may have to spend more actions just crossing intervening space while faster characters may be able to do it in fewer, or possibly run in, whomp, run out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T16:57:39-07:00","id":567130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=566436#post566436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arthur:<br /> <br /> I think you're trying to break a system without the whole thing in front of you. It comes off as a bit silly.<br /> <br /> Yes, there is a critical value in pushing the system to find out what its breaking points are. It isn't an inherently negative judgement because all games have them and it can be very useful to know where they are.<br /> <br /> At the same time, such efforts are only really valuable if you approach the system with good faith. For example:<br /> <br /> If the Director wants a ridiculously slow to act character with this initiative system... don't have him attack the first action he gets. Our giant is dimwitted and slow, and didn't realize a fight was breaking out around him. His first action is to grab his 2 ton club. Bam. All the PCs will get at least one action before he swings that baby at anyone.<br /> <br /> The Director (or ST or GM or whatever) needs to design enemies that actually act mechanically how they are described.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the initiative system, a character that is so slow and uses such and unwieldy weapon that they can only attack every other action, is going to <i>feel</i> a heck of a lot slower than a character that can attack every round. Who goes first in a round is far less meaningful than how much you can get done in one.<br /> <br /> If you want a super-low giant that feels slow, you have to make him actually slow; not just slot him at the end of init.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Scion 1E they had a system for most things like that. They wielded large, heavy <i><b>slow</b></i> weapons, they generally went later because their initiative was generally that much lower. With their lower Dexterity they moved slower. With all of that and the Tick Wheel, it all added up to them actually functioning slower. <br /> <br /> Now without the tick wheel, they will always get to go once a round unless they add weird rules that say 'can only act once every other round'. And that's a cludgy workaround. <br /> <br /> This is a gigantic change to how combat works. And not for the better, IMO.<br /> <br /> (Not to say that the Tick Wheel system didn't have problems. Weapon Speed magical bonuses could get out of control if the Storyteller didn't house rule a minimum tick.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T19:09:16-07:00","id":567237,"title":"","content":"That and weapon speeds add a lot of on the fly addition/subtraction that doesn't seem all that readily workable in my mind. It's one of the many reasons I stopped playing Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T02:12:23-07:00","id":567603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=567130#post567130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Scion 1E they had a system for most things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it did. And the strong consensus on the subject is that the Tick system wasn't worth it. And the old tick-wheel system had flaws with modelling exactly what you were complaining about (aka the big slow guys acting &quot;too fast&quot;). Given your attack speed was not inherently linked to your opening initiative placement, it was entirely possible for the guy with a Speed 8 weapon to win Join Battle and then squish the &quot;speedy&quot; guy with a Speed 3 weapon. As well, a JBA tricked out character could easily force everyone else to be operating on the same opening tick,<br /> <br /> So, we can look at ways to model &quot;slowness&quot; in this system instead. The old system wasn't good, and had plenty of problems directly relating to what actually makes a character &quot;fast.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now without the tick wheel, they will always get to go once a round unless they add weird rules that say 'can only act once every other round'. And that's a cludgy workaround. </div> </div> </div>This seems like you're shifting goal posts. Before, your complaint was not, &quot;the slow characters get to act every round,&quot; but that they might get to go before the faster player characters.<br /> <br /> And really, &quot;this is an insanely unwieldy weapon, it requires you to take a ready weapon action before you can attack with it, even if your character is already holding it,&quot; isn't particularly problematic. Lots of traditional init systems have been doing similar things for decades. Crossbows have, for a very long time, been &quot;balanced&quot; against regular bows by forcing characters to spend combat actions re-readying them. There's no big jump here in terms of simple fixes to designing a character to behave in the system the way it is intended to behave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a gigantic change to how combat works. And not for the better, IMO. </div> </div> </div>Considering both Scion 2e and Exalted 3e are dropping the tick-wheel... I'm not sure how much sympathy you're going to find for this. I think most people (and clearly the developers) felt it caused more trouble than it was worth.<br /> <br /> As well, it is a &quot;gigantic&quot; change... back to what we have with the ST-base systems before Scion 1e/Exalted 2e introducing the tick-wheel style to it. It isn't a complete reversal to classic high-to-low init, but it's not like what the Sardonyx system is doing is some wild and crazy new fangled concept either.<br /> <br /> And, again, you don't know if this is for the better or not yet. You don't have a full system in front of you to play test and get an informed opinion on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T04:39:38-07:00","id":567640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=567130#post567130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Scion 1E they had a system for most things like that. They wielded large, heavy <i><b>slow</b></i> weapons, they generally went later because their initiative was generally that much lower. With their lower Dexterity they moved slower. With all of that and the Tick Wheel, it all added up to them actually functioning slower.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole thing never really worked for Scion. Most characters are strong enough to swing around a comically oversized weapon like a toothpick, and dexterous enough to balance on the head of a pin while doing it. Scion already laughs in the face of physics; making one weapon three ticks slower than another when they both effectively weigh a feather to the person holding it made no sense.<br /> <br /> But what's done is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T17:11:32-07:00","id":568514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=567603#post567603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes it did. And the strong consensus on the subject is that the Tick system wasn't worth it. And the old tick-wheel system had flaws with modelling exactly what you were complaining about (aka the big slow guys acting &quot;too fast&quot;). Given your attack speed was not inherently linked to your opening initiative placement, it was entirely possible for the guy with a Speed 8 weapon to win Join Battle and then squish the &quot;speedy&quot; guy with a Speed 3 weapon. As well, a JBA tricked out character could easily force everyone else to be operating on the same opening tick,<br /> <br /> So, we can look at ways to model &quot;slowness&quot; in this system instead. The old system wasn't good, and had plenty of problems directly relating to what actually makes a character &quot;fast.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to hear where you are getting a 'strong consensus' that the Tick Wheel system wasn't worth it, because my players had little problem with it with a few tweaks. And no, it didn't have what I've stated as a problem. You are comparing apples and oranges. You are positing a low Wits+Awareness initiative w/ someone with high dex, my example rested on 'fast' in wits and dexterity. Yes, you could have an incredibly high wits (or Intelligence with the right knack) character who was not dexterously fast. But if you built your 'squishy fast character' they generally could go decide to go faster if they wanted. <br /> <br /> I don't get where you thought it isn't 'good' it's different.<br /> <br /> I still haven't gotten a good answer why the opposing side going 'next' after the first player is good thematically or dramatically. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=567603#post567603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like you're shifting goal posts. Before, your complaint was not, &quot;the slow characters get to act every round,&quot; but that they might get to go before the faster player characters.<br /> <br /> And really, &quot;this is an insanely unwieldy weapon, it requires you to take a ready weapon action before you can attack with it, even if your character is already holding it,&quot; isn't particularly problematic. Lots of traditional init systems have been doing similar things for decades. Crossbows have, for a very long time, been &quot;balanced&quot; against regular bows by forcing characters to spend combat actions re-readying them. There's no big jump here in terms of simple fixes to designing a character to behave in the system the way it is intended to behave.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an outlier. Most attacks in D&amp;D are usually once a round (or more). Very few spells even have something like a casting time of one round.<br /> <br /> The Tick Wheel system allowed someone with a fast weapon to get in two to three attacks to your big heavy slow bricks one or two attacks. A pure round system discards that entirely. It <i>may</i> be needed to try and balance things, but that can be subjective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=567603#post567603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering both Scion 2e and Exalted 3e are dropping the tick-wheel... I'm not sure how much sympathy you're going to find for this. I think most people (and clearly the developers) felt it caused more trouble than it was worth.<br /> <br /> As well, it is a &quot;gigantic&quot; change... back to what we have with the ST-base systems before Scion 1e/Exalted 2e introducing the tick-wheel style to it. It isn't a complete reversal to classic high-to-low init, but it's not like what the Sardonyx system is doing is some wild and crazy new fangled concept either.<br /> <br /> And, again, you don't know if this is for the better or not yet. You don't have a full system in front of you to play test and get an informed opinion on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not totally adverse to removing the Tick Wheel for a Round system, but the arbitrary nature of who gets to go second really, really bugs me. Because it has nothing to do with initiative or anything, it just has to do with 'the opposing side gets to go now before all the fast people get to go'. That just makes it weird.<br /> <br /> And so I should ignore the teaser previews entirely, even though they are being released just so people can see them and make comments? That comes across as a backhanded 'shut up and don't have an opinion' comment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=567640#post567640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole thing never really worked for Scion. Most characters are strong enough to swing around a comically oversized weapon like a toothpick, and dexterous enough to balance on the head of a pin while doing it. Scion already laughs in the face of physics; making one weapon three ticks slower than another when they both effectively weigh a feather to the person holding it made no sense.<br /> <br /> But what's done is done.</div> </div> </div> </div>It made perfect sense and even fairly well game balance. In fact, even picking up huge things to beat on people was a pretty slow action and might require a set up action. Pick up the Empire State Building while you take some hits, then smash the speedster on your next round.<br /> <br /> That statement doesn't parse as true at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T18:41:59-07:00","id":568587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568514#post568514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to hear where you are getting a 'strong consensus' that the Tick Wheel system wasn't worth it, because my players had little problem with it with a few tweaks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry but the second you added, &quot;with a few tweaks&quot; you lost this point. You're not defending the tick-wheel system once your opening counterargument is, &quot;well my group likes our house ruled version of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> And, &quot;my group likes it, so there isn't a strong consensus against it,&quot; isn't really a functional point either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no, it didn't have what I've stated as a problem. </div> </div> </div>By my reading, you keep changing what the problem is... so that's getting a bit hard to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't get where you thought it isn't 'good' it's different. </div> </div> </div>Where did I get the idea it isn't good?<br /> <br /> Running three Exalted 2e games, playing in another, play testing Scion 1e with my group, and plenty of talking about this one these forums and others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I still haven't gotten a good answer why the opposing side going 'next' after the first player is good thematically or dramatically. </div> </div> </div>Why does everyone keep making the mistake that the Director alternating with the players inherently means opposing sides are the issue? Director NPCs are both friendlies and enemies.<br /> <br /> And it's a good idea from a tonal perspective <i>as a baseline state that can be modified by other mechanics</i> because it helps encourage group oriented tactical thinking. The players can use group tactics that aren't reliant on the dice rolling right or taking massive tactical risks for whatever team work benefit they might get, but still have to be thoughtful about it because they can't just ignore the Director's characters either.<br /> <br /> It also ensures combat maintains a chaotic feel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's an outlier. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but when it's a mechanic that dozens of RPGs have used for this purpose... I don't see how it's an outlier just because it's a rarely used mechanical widget in most of those systems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Tick Wheel system allowed someone with a fast weapon to get in two to three attacks to your big heavy slow bricks one or two attacks. A pure round system discards that entirely. </div> </div> </div>The tick-wheel didn't have some sort of exclusive lock on this. The cWOD system, for example, but rates on guns. Someone dual wielding light semi-auto pistols (with either really high dice-pools or extra action powers) could get up to 8 attacks in a round, while a character with a double barreled shotgun got one. So the opposite direction of my previous example, but the same fundamental mechanical concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because it has nothing to do with initiative or anything, it just has to do with 'the opposing side gets to go now before all the fast people get to go'. </div> </div> </div>1) Initiative is a completely arbitrary fictional concept that means whatever the game wants it to mean.<br /> <br /> 2) It's been made clear that the system will have mechanical ways to represent this; even if they're powers so mundanes don't get them.<br /> <br /> 3) The system isn't trying to model reality. It's pretty clear about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And so I should ignore the teaser previews entirely, even though they are being released just so people can see them and make comments? That comes across as a backhanded 'shut up and don't have an opinion' comment. </div> </div> </div>No. This is you just taking what I said and blowing it way out of proportion. My point is that you need to keep things in perspective. You're not listening to attempts to address your concerns, and you're continually asserting this as valid issues that don't really have any backup in any of the preview material (either the blog posts or comments from the developers).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:12:06-07:00","id":568740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568587#post568587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but the second you added, &quot;with a few tweaks&quot; you lost this point. You're not defending the tick-wheel system once your opening counterargument is, &quot;well my group likes our house ruled version of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> And, &quot;my group likes it, so there isn't a strong consensus against it,&quot; isn't really a functional point either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I houseruled oWoD Werewolf that 1s didn't subtract from successes to make a botch. That does not mean that the entire d10 dice mechanics system was not working or worthwhile. I think the only thing I houseruled the Tick Wheel slightly was so that it wasn't more than 6-8 ticks between everyone, so they could actually all start interacting. (And I'm not even sure on that, it was a long time ago that I ran Scion 1E.)<br /> <br /> (My friends actually then did a statistical study afterwards and showed that the original system in oWoD was a system of failure. You had a higher and higher chance of botching under the original rules the more dice you had and the higher the difficulty. White Wolf actually implemented that rule in the main system later to make it less a game of failure.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568587#post568587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By my reading, you keep changing what the problem is... so that's getting a bit hard to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Says the guy that tried to change my fast-squishy example to his own ends.<br /> <br /> <b>((Oops, my mistake, Heavy Arms. I got you confused with Incedix there for a second. That doesn't change the fact that he tried to mangle the setup to 'prove' his point.))</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568587#post568587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did I get the idea it isn't good?<br /> <br /> Running three Exalted 2e games, playing in another, play testing Scion 1e with my group, and plenty of talking about this one these forums and others.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't change that I see some of the changes as a problem. It isn't that you can't play the game that way, but it's arbitrary and only for 'game fairness' (which is incredibly subjective). Like I said, I'm not against them getting rid of the Tick Wheel. But this goes to another odd mechanic system that I don't feel works for a good dynamic and active system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568587#post568587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does everyone keep making the mistake that the Director alternating with the players inherently means opposing sides are the issue? Director NPCs are both friendlies and enemies.<br /> <br /> And it's a good idea from a tonal perspective <i>as a baseline state that can be modified by other mechanics</i> because it helps encourage group oriented tactical thinking. The players can use group tactics that aren't reliant on the dice rolling right or taking massive tactical risks for whatever team work benefit they might get, but still have to be thoughtful about it because they can't just ignore the Director's characters either.<br /> <br /> It also ensures combat maintains a chaotic feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ie. it arbitrarily decides that the other party gets to go after the fastest initiative. <u>You</u> don't see that as a problem, but I've laid out a few scenarios that actually show potential issues.<br /> <br /> I don't see how letting your opponents or other groups automatically going after the fastest person actually makes it chaotic. In fact, it does quite the opposite. All it does is assure they get an action before someone else. That's it. That's actually more ordered system.<br /> <br /> The Tick Wheel allowed for a greater amount of 'chaotic feel' than that ever would, because your super-fast character made suddenly switch weapons and suddenly start doing slow heavy attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568587#post568587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but when it's a mechanic that dozens of RPGs have used for this purpose... I don't see how it's an outlier just because it's a rarely used mechanical widget in most of those systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an outlier because the mechanic is not regularly used <u>in</u> those systems, not because it exists in several systems. If you made everyone do a load/charge up type action for everything, you'd have an awful lot of unhappy players. In fact, I had a really unhappy player because Exalted 2E magic required a full action just to prepare to cast a spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568587#post568587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tick-wheel didn't have some sort of exclusive lock on this. The cWOD system, for example, but rates on guns. Someone dual wielding light semi-auto pistols (with either really high dice-pools or extra action powers) could get up to 8 attacks in a round, while a character with a double barreled shotgun got one. So the opposite direction of my previous example, but the same fundamental mechanical concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven't heard about multiple actions (or sprays, bursts) whatever in this system yet, so we can't judge it on that. I don't believe it is fully relevant to to a system that modeled where one person could take several quick actions in comparison to a person that could only take slow actions. Using multiple actions to paper over 'speed' ratings is trying to apples and oranges comparisons again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568587#post568587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Initiative is a completely arbitrary fictional concept that means whatever the game wants it to mean.<br /> <br /> 2) It's been made clear that the system will have mechanical ways to represent this; even if they're powers so mundanes don't get them.<br /> <br /> 3) The system isn't trying to model reality. It's pretty clear about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it actually does a worse job of modeling a high action swashbuckler feel than Scion 1E. This is supposed to be an 'Adventure' system that has daredevils and pulp heroes at the low end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568587#post568587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. This is you just taking what I said and blowing it way out of proportion. My point is that you need to keep things in perspective. You're not listening to attempts to address your concerns, and you're continually asserting this as valid issues that don't really have any backup in any of the preview material (either the blog posts or comments from the developers).</div> </div> </div> </div>All I've heard is 'there is no issue, please shut up.' You may not realize that's what I'm hearing, but you are basically belittling my insights and points without even directly addressing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","user":"ArthurHansen","date":". 06-26-2015, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T01:39:17-07:00","id":568932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568740#post568740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I houseruled oWoD Werewolf that 1s didn't subtract from successes to make a botch.</div> </div> </div> </div>And? This means nothing besides the fact that you tend to play WtA with a major house rule (it's a small one to say, but it impacts a huge amount of the system).<br /> <br /> Yes, it doesn't mean the entire d10 ST system was not working. It means the cWOD Rule of 1 doesn't work. Just like the tick-wheel not working doesn't actually condemn all of Exalted 2e/Scion 1e (though both games do plenty of other things with that), it just means that the tick-wheel system doesn't work. Admitting you have to house rule it is admitting it didn't work as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the only thing I houseruled the Tick Wheel slightly was so that it wasn't more than 6-8 ticks between everyone, so they could actually all start interacting. (And I'm not even sure on that, it was a long time ago that I ran Scion 1E.) </div> </div> </div>This doesn't make any sense. Having 8 ticks between two characters is pretty much the maximum possible RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (My friends actually then did a statistical study afterwards and showed that the original system in oWoD was a system of failure. You had a higher and higher chance of botching under the original rules the more dice you had and the higher the difficulty. White Wolf actually implemented that rule in the main system later to make it less a game of failure.) </div> </div> </div>Your friend's stats are wrong (or being cited incorrectly). Most people get this wrong. The cWOD system generally did not have increased rates of botching as dice pools and difficulties increase; there were some &quot;humps&quot; in the curves, not stead increases. What increased consistently was the percentage of non-successful rolls that are botches.<br /> <br /> Basically, the more dice you have, the more likely you are to succeed, but you're also more likely to botch when you don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That doesn't change the fact that he tried to mangle the setup to 'prove' his point </div> </div> </div>Great... how about my actual point then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>You</u> don't see that as a problem, but I've laid out a few scenarios that actually show potential issues. </div> </div> </div>Which have been thoroughly addressed and demonstrated to not actually raise cohesive or significant concerns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see how letting your opponents or other groups automatically going after the fastest person actually makes it chaotic. </div> </div> </div>Hence the word &quot;feel&quot; being in there. All initiative systems are about creating order in something that supposed to feel chaotic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Tick Wheel allowed for a greater amount of 'chaotic feel' than that ever would, because your super-fast character made suddenly switch weapons and suddenly start doing slow heavy attacks. </div> </div> </div>That's not chaos, that's shifting tactics. The tick-wheel gives low Speed characters massive amounts of control over the pace and flow of combat. The preview Sardonyx system gives ways for players to control the system, but by default ensures there's less overall control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's an outlier because the mechanic is not regularly used <u>in</u> those systems, not because it exists in several systems. </div> </div> </div>Semantic games that don't even really seem to get what the word outlier means.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter. It's standard mechanic. It's not strange, special, particularly clunky, or anything of the sort that you're trying to paint it with that word.<br /> <br /> And it's no different than going in the other direction with things like weapon rates. The point is, you can do things like control number of attacks/actions in a round that has a massive impact on the feeling of &quot;speed&quot; of a character that has nothing to do with initiative order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, I had a really unhappy player because Exalted 2E magic required a full action just to prepare to cast a spell. </div> </div> </div>Feature, not a bug. Exalted has always had Sorcery take time in combat because it isn't meant to be D&amp;D style combat magic; that's what Charms are form. It was designed from 1e to not be there for throwing fireballs at people and was designed to discourage such uses. Use in active combat was meant to be situational and tactical; and making it hard to do in combat is part of making it do that.<br /> <br /> Your players weren't unhappy with the rules, but with the game design intent itself (which goes back to Exalted 1e anyway).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using multiple actions to paper over 'speed' ratings is trying to apples and oranges comparisons again. </div> </div> </div>Labeling any argument you don't like &quot;apples and oranges&quot; isn't very effective. It just makes it sound like you don't know what that phrase means, and are reaching for a way to dodge points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but it actually does a worse job of modeling a high action swashbuckler feel than Scion 1E. This is supposed to be an 'Adventure' system that has daredevils and pulp heroes at the low end. </div> </div> </div>You have no proof of this. You haven't even shown a good educated guess as to where this will be a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All I've heard is 'there is no issue, please shut up.' You may not realize that's what I'm hearing, but you are basically belittling my insights and points without even directly addressing them. </div> </div> </div>I have been given little reason to care. I'm currently feeling that you would &quot;hear&quot; this regardless of what I've posted. Why should I change how I'm saying things if you're going to read under the lens of some weird persecution complex? It's not going to matter how I say it anyway.<br /> <br /> You're hearing what you want to hear. Try hearing what people are actually saying.<br /> <br /> And really... don't try to get into some sort of tonal critique while tossing around phrases like, &quot;belittling my insights.&quot; You're basically saying that you believe that you have already &quot;won&quot; an argument, and disagreeing with you makes me a whiner who's being mean out of spite for losing, rather than expressing that you have observations about the previews which are being discussed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T17:29:53-07:00","id":569805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568932#post568932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And? This means nothing besides the fact that you tend to play WtA with a major house rule (it's a small one to say, but it impacts a huge amount of the system).<br /> <br /> Yes, it doesn't mean the entire d10 ST system was not working. It means the cWOD Rule of 1 doesn't work. Just like the tick-wheel not working doesn't actually condemn all of Exalted 2e/Scion 1e (though both games do plenty of other things with that), it just means that the tick-wheel system doesn't work. Admitting you have to house rule it is admitting it didn't work as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nor does you condemning my experience with a Tick Wheel because we found it to work fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568932#post568932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't make any sense. Having 8 ticks between two characters is pretty much the maximum possible RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said 'If I recall correctly'. I haven't actually played Scion for quite a while. Mostly because I dropped out of my groups games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568932#post568932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your friend's stats are wrong (or being cited incorrectly). Most people get this wrong. The cWOD system generally did not have increased rates of botching as dice pools and difficulties increase; there were some &quot;humps&quot; in the curves, not stead increases. What increased consistently was the percentage of non-successful rolls that are botches.<br /> <br /> Basically, the more dice you have, the more likely you are to succeed, but you're also more likely to botch when you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The two of them are math nerds and had the paperwork to prove it, so I'm going to have to say that I trust their word over your off hand numbers supposition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568932#post568932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great... how about my actual point then?</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual point was that you were referring to someone else moving the goal post? My point was only clarified and still sees an issue with how the new initiative system (seems to have) has issues with multiple players with high initiatives being shafted by the fact that only one person on your side can 'go fast' because no matter how faster they are, the other actors get to go second by the raw explanation.<br /> <br /> And that is potentially lethal to squishy fast characters (which is one of the fairly typical archetypes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568932#post568932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which have been thoroughly addressed and demonstrated to not actually raise cohesive or significant concerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, you stating that everyone is 'fine' with playing it is perfectly countered by 'everyone I knew was perfectly fine with playing with a tick wheel'. So your point basically boils down to 'you shouldn't have an opinion.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568932#post568932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence the word &quot;feel&quot; being in there. All initiative systems are about creating order in something that supposed to feel chaotic.<br /> <br /> That's not chaos, that's shifting tactics. The tick-wheel gives low Speed characters massive amounts of control over the pace and flow of combat. The preview Sardonyx system gives ways for players to control the system, but by default ensures there's less overall control.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that feel is very subjective compared to actually having different speed actions that can dramatically impact things rather than everyone goes around in a form of round robin. You don't actually have an facts to back that up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568932#post568932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Semantic games that don't even really seem to get what the word outlier means.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter. It's standard mechanic. It's not strange, special, particularly clunky, or anything of the sort that you're trying to paint it with that word.<br /> <br /> And it's no different than going in the other direction with things like weapon rates. The point is, you can do things like control number of attacks/actions in a round that has a massive impact on the feeling of &quot;speed&quot; of a character that has nothing to do with initiative order.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are still trying to state this as fact without any information on multiple actions. So you have that as a solution without any information for sure in that it is in the case. Or have you already seen a Teaser that actually has multiple actions laid out?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568932#post568932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feature, not a bug. Exalted has always had Sorcery take time in combat because it isn't meant to be D&amp;D style combat magic; that's what Charms are form. It was designed from 1e to not be there for throwing fireballs at people and was designed to discourage such uses. Use in active combat was meant to be situational and tactical; and making it hard to do in combat is part of making it do that.<br /> <br /> Your players weren't unhappy with the rules, but with the game design intent itself (which goes back to Exalted 1e anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, they are both truisms, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568932#post568932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Labeling any argument you don't like &quot;apples and oranges&quot; isn't very effective. It just makes it sound like you don't know what that phrase means, and are reaching for a way to dodge points.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, labeling things that aren't actually that similar as different is &quot;apples and oranges&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568932#post568932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have no proof of this. You haven't even shown a good educated guess as to where this will be a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've laid out an exact scenario that you have not poked any direct hole in as an example of a problem. How that is not an 'educated guess' means you have decided to disregard anything I say, no matter what it's worth might actually be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=568932#post568932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been given little reason to care. I'm currently feeling that you would &quot;hear&quot; this regardless of what I've posted. Why should I change how I'm saying things if you're going to read under the lens of some weird persecution complex? It's not going to matter how I say it anyway.<br /> <br /> You're hearing what you want to hear. Try hearing what people are actually saying.<br /> <br /> And really... don't try to get into some sort of tonal critique while tossing around phrases like, &quot;belittling my insights.&quot; You're basically saying that you believe that you have already &quot;won&quot; an argument, and disagreeing with you makes me a whiner who's being mean out of spite for losing, rather than expressing that you have observations about the previews which are being discussed.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm bringing up points and issues. You have basically told me 'it doesn't matter, it works because people can play it as a game'. Which doesn't actually mean it isn't a problem, it just means that people are willing to put up with issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T22:41:28-07:00","id":569973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=569805#post569805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nor does you condemning my experience with a Tick Wheel because we found it to work fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, 1 point in the, &quot;hearing what you want to hear and ignoring what was said,&quot; column.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why I said 'If I recall correctly'. I haven't actually played Scion for quite a while. Mostly because I dropped out of my groups games. </div> </div> </div>That still leaves us with no idea of what tweaks were made, and whether or not they're significant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The two of them are math nerds and had the paperwork to prove it, so I'm going to have to say that I trust their word over your off hand numbers supposition. </div> </div> </div>&quot;My friends are math nerds and you disagree with me, so I'm right.&quot; O...k...<br /> <br /> Fine.. math:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://axiscity.hexamon.net/users/isomage/rpgmath/wod/probabilities.txt\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://axiscity.hexamon.net/users/isomage/rpgmath/wod/probabilities.txt\" target=\"_blank\"> Loading... </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://axiscity.hexamon.net/users/isomage/rpgmath/wod/probabilities.txt\" target=\"_blank\"> http://axiscity.hexamon.net/users/isomage/rpgmath/wod/probabilities.txt </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Note the first column. For difficulties 2-6, botches consistently decrease in probability with more dice. For difficulties 7-8, there is a bump up from 1 die to 2 dice, and then consistent decrease from there with more dice. At difficulty 9 you go up from 1 to 4 dice, and after that the probability of botch consistently decreases. At difficulty 10, you go up from 1 to 6 dice, and after that the probability of botching consistently decreases.<br /> <br /> They &quot;had&quot; paperwork. I have it. So... you can stop treating me like I can't just freaking Google a cWOD probability chart well enough to make a simple point<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point was only clarified and still sees an issue with how the new initiative system (seems to have) has issues with multiple players with high initiatives being shafted by the fact that only one person on your side can 'go fast' because no matter how faster they are, the other actors get to go second by the raw explanation.<br /> <br /> And that is potentially lethal to squishy fast characters (which is one of the fairly typical archetypes). </div> </div> </div>And this remains addressed:<br /> <br /> 1) There are multiple ways the system represents &quot;fast&quot; besides &quot;reaction time.&quot; As Malcolm noted, dodging is a big one of them.<br /> <br /> 2) There are tools we already know about such as Focus that allow alterations to the round order.<br /> <br /> 3) There are tools we can assume safely that the Director can use to avoid this easily (ex: taking time to &quot;power up&quot; an attack or whatever)..<br /> <br /> 4) We know the developers (because they said so here) plan on having powers that interact with action order; it is safe to assume speedy characters will have access to them.<br /> <br /> If your issue is solely the PC &gt; Director &gt; PC order of combat, this thread has thoroughly demonstrated that this shouldn't be an issue when it comes to characters with speed powers. At mundane/daredevil level play, where such powers aren't as likely to exist, it is also the point where such drastic differences in action order are less jarring. To use your own example of zombies, even in classic shambler zombie movies, the zombies don't always &quot;act last&quot; despite being sluggish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Um, you stating that everyone is 'fine' with playing it is perfectly countered by 'everyone I knew was perfectly fine with playing with a tick wheel'. So your point basically boils down to 'you shouldn't have an opinion.' </div> </div> </div>2 points in the hearing-what-you-want bin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that feel is very subjective compared to actually having different speed actions that can dramatically impact things rather than everyone goes around in a form of round robin. You don't actually have an facts to back that up. </div> </div> </div>3 points...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are still trying to state this as fact without any information on multiple actions. So you have that as a solution without any information for sure in that it is in the case. Or have you already seen a Teaser that actually has multiple actions laid out? </div> </div> </div>4 points.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't need the teasers for me to say that a Director character can be modeled such that they need to &quot;reload&quot; between attacks because I want them to feel really slow. I know I can do that from the Teasers because I, as the Director, can have my character act however I design them to within the system to suit my needs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, labeling things that aren't actually that similar as different is &quot;apples and oranges&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Are you familiar with the Fallacy Fallacy?<br /> <br /> Also 5 points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've laid out an exact scenario that you have not poked any direct hole in as an example of a problem. </div> </div> </div>6 points (I did the Superman and Flash vs. zombies, remember?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, I'm bringing up points and issues. </div> </div> </div>That's your goal. But while you're busy telling me what you hear from my posts, I'm letting you know what I hear from yours in return, and I'm even being much more specific about it by putting a quoted phrase up for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have basically told me 'it doesn't matter, it works because people can play it as a game'. Which doesn't actually mean it isn't a problem, it just means that people are willing to put up with issues. </div> </div> </div>And 7 total points in the, &quot;you're hearing what you want to hear, not what people are saying!&quot; tally.<br /> <br /> This might go better if you stop that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T10:55:50-07:00","id":570339,"title":"","content":"Wow, your grid actually shows that you can't botch with more than three dice at a standard difficulty. Your statistics model is very simple. Because there is always a chance you could roll all 1s on 10 dice. I still trust my friend far over your example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T13:01:25-07:00","id":570467,"title":"","content":"Um... what?<br /> <br /> If you want to see what the odds of botching with 3 dice at the standard difficulty of 6 in there. You start with the chart that says &quot;Difficulty 6.&quot; Go down to &quot;3&quot; and over one to the &quot;Botch&quot; column. It says 6.10, or 6.10% odds of botching. Not zero.<br /> <br /> As well, anytime those charts say 0.00 that does not mean, &quot;can't botch.&quot; (or whatever the column is; though sometimes it is actually zero) it means, &quot;the odds of botching is less than 0.005%&quot; Because rounding and significant figures is a thing that computer programs do.<br /> <br /> Seriously though what are you trying to prove?<br /> <br /> If you're trying to make us think more highly of your observations of the Sardonyx previews, you're not going to get there by showing you can't read those charts correctly. And you're really not going to get there by playing your mistakes in reading them as a reason to dismiss me and &quot;trust your friends.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T17:38:02-07:00","id":570733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=570467#post570467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... what?<br /> <br /> If you want to see what the odds of botching with 3 dice at the standard difficulty of 6 in there. You start with the chart that says &quot;Difficulty 6.&quot; Go down to &quot;3&quot; and over one to the &quot;Botch&quot; column. It says 6.10, or 6.10% odds of botching. Not zero.<br /> <br /> As well, anytime those charts say 0.00 that does not mean, &quot;can't botch.&quot; (or whatever the column is; though sometimes it is actually zero) it means, &quot;the odds of botching is less than 0.005%&quot; Because rounding and significant figures is a thing that computer programs do.<br /> <br /> Seriously though what are you trying to prove?<br /> <br /> If you're trying to make us think more highly of your observations of the Sardonyx previews, you're not going to get there by showing you can't read those charts correctly. And you're really not going to get there by playing your mistakes in reading them as a reason to dismiss me and &quot;trust your friends.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I misread the chart. Well, I don't think it's well labeled (it's hard to tell). So the first column is supposed to be difficulty and the +number is the dice?<br /> <br /> It still shows that as the difficulty goes higher, that your chance of botching decreases. And that <u>shouldn't</u> happen.<br /> <br /> What I really brought up the dice points was that back then in oWoD 1E, it was a dice system of failure. It did not promote succeeding if you were really higher skilled (ie better dice pool). The harder difficulties and more dice did not actually balance out correctly when 1s subtracted. Removing 1s from subtracting immediately gave everyone a better chance of succeeding. And players like to succeed at heroic actions.<br /> <br /> The new initiative mechanic explicitly makes you less effective by default because you have to choose between the <u>worse</u> of two dice pools.<br /> <br /> And it's the thought process <u><i><b>behind</b></i> </u>that decision that worries me. Because they are too worried about limiting players or 'fair rules' or something, not in letting them have fun with their characters.<br /> <br /> If they had said either or, whichever is better I wouldn't have a problem. Along with some comments on RPG.net about the fact that some basic combat actions are being spread among several different dice pools, they are imposing another limit in 'being good' at something instead of just using a numbered modifier for those different actions.<br /> <br /> Then you add the 'other side' always going second and it's starting to look like they are doing rules changes just to do things &quot;different&quot;. Different can be good, but too different and suddenly you have something <u>entirely</u> different.<br /> <br /> And that way leads to the darkness known as D&amp;D 4E. Or the jump from oWoD to NuWoD, which alienated a pretty large section of the playerbase (including myself).<br /> <br /> This is looking less and less like a second edition and just an entirely different game that sorta has the same setting. The only thing that seems to be staying the same is... it used d10s.<br /> <br /> {add} Of course, if they really did the NuWoD treatment, we'll find out that the entire idea of Titans breaking free and it's the end of times is being thrown out and it's now all just politics between different pantheons. We don't need clear cut 'bad guys' and such. I mean, the Camarilla and the Sabat were just stupid ideas. Who needs them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","user":"ArthurHansen","date":". 06-27-2015, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T20:51:20-07:00","id":570863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=570733#post570733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't think it's well labeled (it's hard to tell). So the first column is supposed to be difficulty and the +number is the dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>.... there's 9 charts, each labelled with &quot;Difficulty X.&quot; The Difficulty is based on the chart. The first column is the number of dice.<br /> <br /> I seriously am not sure why this is difficult. And I gave an example of how to use it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It still shows that as the difficulty goes higher, that your chance of botching decreases. And that <u>shouldn't</u> happen. </div> </div> </div>No, for the same number of dice, increasing difficulty alone increases the odds of botching unless you're rolling 1 die (which is always 10%). That's in the charts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I really brought up the dice points was that back then in oWoD 1E, it was a dice system of failure. It did not promote succeeding if you were really higher skilled (ie better dice pool). </div> </div> </div>Except it does. More dice = better odds of success. Whether it's good enough for your tastes doesn't change the math. It isn't a &quot;system of failure&quot; where you pay XP to do worse. It's a system with significant diminishing returns. You pay more and more XP, for dice that have less and less impact. But you're betting better for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Removing 1s from subtracting immediately gave everyone a better chance of succeeding. And players like to succeed at heroic actions. </div> </div> </div>Well... duh? That's why the non-cWOD games made the rules with 1s less punishing. Removing 1s subtracting successes makes dice more potent. That was never in contention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The new initiative mechanic explicitly makes you less effective by default because you have to choose between the <u>worse</u> of two dice pools. </div> </div> </div>And that's a complete non-sequitur. And yes, you pick the lowest of two dice pools. However as a basic mechanical function, we have Enhancements. So even with a lower dice pool you can still massively out preform other people if you have access to lots of bonuses to it. The Sardonyx spoilers have made it clear that dice pool is not the sole arbiter of effectiveness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it's the thought process <u><i><b>behind</b></i> </u>that decision that worries me. Because they are too worried about limiting players or 'fair rules' or something, not in letting them have fun with their characters. </div> </div> </div>I don't recall any of the developers saying anything of the sort. And most of them have said things to the exact opposite. That powers will do things like let you be awesome at stuff without as much investment in Attributes and Skills that a mundane will need.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you add the 'other side' always going second and it's starting to look like they are doing rules changes just to do things &quot;different&quot;. Different can be good, but too different and suddenly you have something <u>entirely</u> different. </div> </div> </div>Again, what we know so far, is that &quot;always going second&quot; is &quot;always without Focus or powers coming into play.&quot;<br /> <br /> And &quot;looking like they're doing something just to be different&quot; is kind of silly considering there are a few others games out there that use initiative systems that are more negotiated rather than purely mechanical-order determined. And who cares if it is &quot;entirely&quot; different if it works?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that way leads to the darkness known as D&amp;D 4E. Or the jump from oWoD to NuWoD, which alienated a pretty large section of the playerbase (including myself). </div> </div> </div>I doubt many people would agree with either of those assessments. Mostly because neither D&amp;D 4e or the nWOD were made &quot;just to be different.&quot; New editions with new rules does risk alienating players. The devs know this. Until we at least have a playable amount of information from the previews, we can't say for sure if we like them or not. And some people are doing to dislike the new edition of Scion regardless of what people think of the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is looking less and less like a second edition and just an entirely different game that sorta has the same setting. The only thing that seems to be staying the same is... it used d10s. </div> </div> </div>They're writing a custom system for it... of course it's going to be a more significant change than going from, say, VtM Rev to V20.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D editions have had very drastic changes between editions. They're all still D&amp;D.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T20:57:40-07:00","id":570868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=570733#post570733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">{add} Of course, if they really did the NuWoD treatment, we'll find out that the entire idea of Titans breaking free and it's the end of times is being thrown out and it's now all just politics between different pantheons. We don't need clear cut 'bad guys' and such. I mean, the Camarilla and the Sabat were just stupid ideas. Who needs them?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Please review rule #3: Respect other people's preferences. Edition warring is a violation of this rule.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T22:15:49-07:00","id":570979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=570863#post570863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... there's 9 charts, each labelled with &quot;Difficulty X.&quot; The Difficulty is based on the chart. The first column is the number of dice.<br /> <br /> I seriously am not sure why this is difficult. And I gave an example of how to use it.<br /> <br /> No, for the same number of dice, increasing difficulty alone increases the odds of botching unless you're rolling 1 die (which is always 10%). That's in the charts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really isn't what I was seeing there, but I'm not going to argue math or go bug my friend to find her information<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=570863#post570863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's a complete non-sequitur. And yes, you pick the lowest of two dice pools. However as a basic mechanical function, we have Enhancements. So even with a lower dice pool you can still massively out preform other people if you have access to lots of bonuses to it. The Sardonyx spoilers have made it clear that dice pool is not the sole arbiter of effectiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>You basically decided that my point had absolutely no merit by stating an entirely different mechanic will definitely fix it.... So now your dice don't even matter, because everyone will just have to use Enhancements. Unless everyone uses all the same enhancements and now the dice actually matter. <br /> <br /> I will admit I haven't deeply thought on the Focus issue, but I read just enough to go WTF!?!? when it said if you have Focus, you can't only fail and you will botch if you don't succeed. That seemed like an incredibly bad concept and design that punishes the players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=570863#post570863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall any of the developers saying anything of the sort. And most of them have said things to the exact opposite. That powers will do things like let you be awesome at stuff without as much investment in Attributes and Skills that a mundane will need.</div> </div> </div> </div>The developers may not realize they are actually doing it or even think in that way. I'm pretty positive that the oWoD 1.0 developers never actively decided that they wanted to put in 1s to make it a system that makes players failures.<br /> <br /> This is what I am inferring by what they are showing us in these teasers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=570863#post570863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, what we know so far, is that &quot;always going second&quot; is &quot;always without Focus or powers coming into play.&quot;<br /> <br /> And &quot;looking like they're doing something just to be different&quot; is kind of silly considering there are a few others games out there that use initiative systems that are more negotiated rather than purely mechanical-order determined. And who cares if it is &quot;entirely&quot; different if it works?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can play a game with any initiative system (or none even.) That does not mean all of them work well in all situations or with all games. Just throwing out that 'well anything can work' isn't really pointing out issue in the system. Or possible ways to fix it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=570863#post570863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt many people would agree with either of those assessments. Mostly because neither D&amp;D 4e or the nWOD were made &quot;just to be different.&quot; New editions with new rules does risk alienating players. The devs know this. Until we at least have a playable amount of information from the previews, we can't say for sure if we like them or not. And some people are doing to dislike the new edition of Scion regardless of what people think of the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to explain in an analogy that hopefully doesn't get the mods more upset. D&amp;D to AD&amp;D 3.5E and D&amp;D 5E are mostly derivative. While they may have introduced or tweaked rules between the systems, you can see how they evolved. The same for the version of oWoD. What D&amp;D 4E and NuWoD did were fairly drastic changes and they play very, very differently. That is not to say that some people don't like them. There are also people that refuse to play anything but the very first system they ever did (I actually knew a guy that refused to every play anything but AD&amp;D. Everything D&amp;D 2E and later he ignored, because he knew the rules and had all the books.)<br /> <br /> The analogy part of this is that derivative versions I'll liken to TV shows. Battlestar Galactica is a good example. The first series had several seasons, that had broadly the same mechanics and same characters and many people have very fond memories. NuBSG on the other hand is very, very different with characters that have the same names, but the mechanics are very different, tenor and the background is different even though across its seasons, it matched its own tones and style consistently. But you really can't compare them too well, because in so many ways they are very, very different.<br /> <br /> The differences of course with games with rules, if you change things too drastically, you end up with forever version 1.0 Beta problems (which Scion 1E was a bit of a victim of.) But drastically changing the mechanics as Scion 2E appears to be doing is basically being a 'do-over' with a new version 1.0 Beta. Even more so if they do decide to seriously tweak the background and settings dramatically.<br /> <br /> I've tended to see in RPGs that the derivative changes tend to be for the better, because they fix a lot of issues with limited introduction of new problems. You don't have things like D&amp;D 4E where everyone class plays like a spellcaster, excepting some of the spellcasters. Or that Dragonlance cardgame RPG that was technically D&amp;D, but played nothing at all like any other D&amp;D games. It didn't even have character sheets that allowed you to really advance your character.<br /> <br /> :-/<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=570863#post570863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're writing a custom system for it... of course it's going to be a more significant change than going from, say, VtM Rev to V20.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D editions have had very drastic changes between editions. They're all still D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd note that while D&amp;D 4E may have been a version, it was a very drastic difference that did not do a good job of replacing 3.5E. I think TSR/Hasbro has even stated that this was a problem and why D&amp;D 5E is much more similar to D&amp;D 3.5E. The very odd D&amp;D card game RPG they had after one of the resets in Dragonlance was also a 'far too different' change.<br /> <br /> That isn't to say they have no redeeming qualities or rules. I think D&amp;D 5E is stealing some of the better rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=570868#post570868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">Please review rule #3: Respect other people's preferences. Edition warring is a violation of this rule.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm not really trying to say one is better than the other, I'm trying to use them as an example of <i>why</i> some of the difference between oWoD and NuWoD can make people feel like that. And why I feel that is applicable here in this situation with Scion 1E and the now jump to Scion 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T23:32:52-07:00","id":571038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=570979#post570979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You basically decided that my point had absolutely no merit by stating an entirely different mechanic will definitely fix it.... So now your dice don't even matter, because everyone will just have to use Enhancements. Unless everyone uses all the same enhancements and now the dice actually matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>For fuck's sake...<br /> <br /> Can we please have an actual conversation here?<br /> <br /> <b>Stop ignoring what I said for whatever twisted nonsense you've decided I &quot;really&quot; meant.</b><br /> <br /> I provided a counter-point to your point. That Enhancements, a standard part of the core Sardoynx resolution mechanic, is a major influence on character effectiveness. Since characters get +X bonus successes for various actions, it is very easy for your lower dice pool to be your better dice pool in application. If I have 5 dice or 8 dice for my two initiative dice pools, but I get +4 successes to the first, and +1 success to the second, it is highly likely I'm actually better off with the five dice over the eight dice (Tier impacts this a bit since the TN changes things). If we're at TN 8, I'd average 6 success with the lower rating, and just 4.2 success with the higher dice pool. Though there's something the rules don't address (in normal resolution Enhancements don't count if you don't roll at least one success, and we don't know if init is an exception to that, but generally speaking the odds of rolling fails are pretty small), it remains true from the previews so far that picking the lowest of two pools is not an inherent reduction in actual effectiveness.<br /> <br /> It's not a &quot;different mechanic will fix it.&quot; The core resolution mechanics are robust enough to address this.<br /> <br /> The whole hyperbolic thing with &quot;dice don't even matter&quot; is ridiculous and nothing in what I said. Dice matter, but Enhancements matters as well. That's why I said, &quot;The Sardonyx spoilers have made it clear that dice pool is not the sole arbiter of effectiveness.&quot; Not &quot;dice pools don't matter,&quot; but that dice pools are not the only thing that matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will admit I haven't deeply thought on the Focus issue, but I read just enough to go WTF!?!? when it said if you have Focus, you can't only fail and you will botch if you don't succeed. That seemed like an incredibly bad concept and design that punishes the players. </div> </div> </div>And... is there any question on why I'm frustrated yet?<br /> <br /> I've been saying &quot;Focus&quot; constantly in this. You want us to take your analysis of the initiative system seriously, but you also haven't put thought into a major component of it?<br /> <br /> Yes, having Focus has a drawback in all non-successful rolls are botches. It also has a large number of bonuses; including getting to go whenever you want in the round. Which is key to a full examination of the spoilers.<br /> <br /> Saying it &quot;punishes&quot; players shows no in-depth reading at all. &quot;Here's a pile of bonuses but they come with a major drawback,&quot; is not a punishment. It's a trade off. And one that generally gives far more than it risks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The developers may not realize they are actually doing it or even think in that way. I'm pretty positive that the oWoD 1.0 developers never actively decided that they wanted to put in 1s to make it a system that makes players failures. </div> </div> </div>You can't have it both ways. You can't claim the developers are designing with specific goals/motivations, and they say &quot;well they might not be,&quot;<br /> <br /> And the cWOD developers didn't make a system that makes players failures. They made a system that doesn't readily make for heroic/awesome effectiveness. Which makes sense given its intent.<br /> <br /> Also, you can't say you're not going to argue something any more, and then treat it like you won the argument. If you're not going to argue the math of the cWOD system and if it makes it a game of &quot;player failure,&quot; stop treating it as fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is what I am inferring by what they are showing us in these teasers. </div> </div> </div>You haven't exactly provided a lot of justification for those assumptions.<br /> <br /> What are you claiming actually shows this?<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, your argument is, &quot;changes can be bad, I don't like some of these changes, therefore those changes are objectively bad and the developers are either maliciously or incompetently making a game that only exists to spit on Scion 1e.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can play a game with any initiative system (or none even.) That does not mean all of them work well in all situations or with all games. Just throwing out that 'well anything can work' isn't really pointing out issue in the system. Or possible ways to fix it. </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what this has to do with what I said.<br /> <br /> As well, I don't see any issues with the basic concepts of the Sardonyx initiative system (there's plenty of room for it to not live up to its potential), so I have nothing to present fixes for.<br /> <br /> And you haven't exactly been posting &quot;fixes&quot; for any of the issues you're seeing. You mostly seem to just want to plug the tick-wheel back into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The differences of course with games with rules, if you change things too drastically, you end up with forever version 1.0 Beta problems (which Scion 1E was a bit of a victim of.) But drastically changing the mechanics as Scion 2E appears to be doing is basically being a 'do-over' with a new version 1.0 Beta. Even more so if they do decide to seriously tweak the background and settings dramatically. </div> </div> </div>The analogy fails pretty hard considering that Sardonyx isn't just for Scion. It's a core engine for multiple separate properties.<br /> <br /> The previews aren't even 1.0 Beta. Yes, there's a possibility that the final versions when Scion 2e comes out suffer 1.0 problems. In fact, it's pretty likely there will be some. Even really polished games have mistakes in first first run. But the level of &quot;dramatic&quot; change from Scion 1e's systems is irrelevant to this process. The Sardonyx system is a new system being built, not the Scion 1e system being reworked. How dramatically different is is from Scion 1e matters to the likelihood of 1.0 problems as how dramatically different it is from D&amp;D 1e. It's not being built on either game as a backbone.<br /> <br /> And letting concerns about changes to the background/setting are irrelevant to an analysis of the mechanics for the game engine previews. Whatever they decide to do along those regards doesn't impact if the initiative system works well or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T14:04:59-07:00","id":571858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=571038#post571038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For fuck's sake...<br /> <br /> Can we please have an actual conversation here?<br /> <br /> <b>Stop ignoring what I said for whatever twisted nonsense you've decided I &quot;really&quot; meant.</b><br /> <br /> I provided a counter-point to your point. That Enhancements, a standard part of the core Sardoynx resolution mechanic, is a major influence on character effectiveness. Since characters get +X bonus successes for various actions, it is very easy for your lower dice pool to be your better dice pool in application. If I have 5 dice or 8 dice for my two initiative dice pools, but I get +4 successes to the first, and +1 success to the second, it is highly likely I'm actually better off with the five dice over the eight dice (Tier impacts this a bit since the TN changes things). If we're at TN 8, I'd average 6 success with the lower rating, and just 4.2 success with the higher dice pool. Though there's something the rules don't address (in normal resolution Enhancements don't count if you don't roll at least one success, and we don't know if init is an exception to that, but generally speaking the odds of rolling fails are pretty small), it remains true from the previews so far that picking the lowest of two pools is not an inherent reduction in actual effectiveness.<br /> <br /> It's not a &quot;different mechanic will fix it.&quot; The core resolution mechanics are robust enough to address this.<br /> <br /> The whole hyperbolic thing with &quot;dice don't even matter&quot; is ridiculous and nothing in what I said. Dice matter, but Enhancements matters as well. That's why I said, &quot;The Sardonyx spoilers have made it clear that dice pool is not the sole arbiter of effectiveness.&quot; Not &quot;dice pools don't matter,&quot; but that dice pools are not the only thing that matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet the way you stated it came across as 'it doesn't matter that the developers are forcing people to use the least amount of dice possible because of X'. That's my problem with your examples. You are ignoring that even just the the concept of them saying 'use the smaller of two dice pools' is in any way shape or form of a problem. <br /> <br /> <i><b>That's what's pissing me off about your responses.</b></i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=571038#post571038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... is there any question on why I'm frustrated yet?<br /> <br /> I've been saying &quot;Focus&quot; constantly in this. You want us to take your analysis of the initiative system seriously, but you also haven't put thought into a major component of it?<br /> <br /> Yes, having Focus has a drawback in all non-successful rolls are botches. It also has a large number of bonuses; including getting to go whenever you want in the round. Which is key to a full examination of the spoilers.<br /> <br /> Saying it &quot;punishes&quot; players shows no in-depth reading at all. &quot;Here's a pile of bonuses but they come with a major drawback,&quot; is not a punishment. It's a trade off. And one that generally gives far more than it risks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to just disagree on this at principal, but you obviously feel that no one can have any opinion on not liking this initiative mechanic. So it doesn't matter to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=571038#post571038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't have it both ways. You can't claim the developers are designing with specific goals/motivations, and they say &quot;well they might not be,&quot;<br /> <br /> And the cWOD developers didn't make a system that makes players failures. They made a system that doesn't readily make for heroic/awesome effectiveness. Which makes sense given its intent.<br /> <br /> Also, you can't say you're not going to argue something any more, and then treat it like you won the argument. If you're not going to argue the math of the cWOD system and if it makes it a game of &quot;player failure,&quot; stop treating it as fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even you noted that subtracting 1s heavily affected 'success' in cWoD, making players fail more. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=571038#post571038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You haven't exactly provided a lot of justification for those assumptions.<br /> <br /> What are you claiming actually shows this?<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, your argument is, &quot;changes can be bad, I don't like some of these changes, therefore those changes are objectively bad and the developers are either maliciously or incompetently making a game that only exists to spit on Scion 1e.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's incredibly dismissive. Again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=571038#post571038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea what this has to do with what I said.<br /> <br /> As well, I don't see any issues with the basic concepts of the Sardonyx initiative system (there's plenty of room for it to not live up to its potential), so I have nothing to present fixes for.<br /> <br /> And you haven't exactly been posting &quot;fixes&quot; for any of the issues you're seeing. You mostly seem to just want to plug the tick-wheel back into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd want a system that actually let's people that roll higher go first. That's pretty simple. And doesn't require a tick wheel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=571038#post571038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The analogy fails pretty hard considering that Sardonyx isn't just for Scion. It's a core engine for multiple separate properties.<br /> <br /> The previews aren't even 1.0 Beta. Yes, there's a possibility that the final versions when Scion 2e comes out suffer 1.0 problems. In fact, it's pretty likely there will be some. Even really polished games have mistakes in first first run. But the level of &quot;dramatic&quot; change from Scion 1e's systems is irrelevant to this process. The Sardonyx system is a new system being built, not the Scion 1e system being reworked. How dramatically different is is from Scion 1e matters to the likelihood of 1.0 problems as how dramatically different it is from D&amp;D 1e. It's not being built on either game as a backbone.<br /> <br /> And letting concerns about changes to the background/setting are irrelevant to an analysis of the mechanics for the game engine previews. Whatever they decide to do along those regards doesn't impact if the initiative system works well or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I noted that if they made as dramatic a change to the background and setting <i><u>on top</u></i> of massive mechanics changes, they are setting themselves up to a similar situation that D&amp;D 4E and NuWoD ran into.<br /> <br /> If they are specifically trying to do that, they shouldn't be trying to call is Scion 2E, they should be very upfront about calling it 'an entirely new game that shares some background assumptions about being a modern mythology.' Clear communication in that direction can stave off a lot of heartache and anger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T18:42:54-07:00","id":572068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=571858#post571858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are ignoring that even just the the concept of them saying 'use the smaller of two dice pools' is in any way shape or form of a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that:<br /> <br /> 1) There is nothing inherently problematic about &quot;use the lower of two&quot; mechanics.<br /> <br /> 2) There is nothing in the previews that indicates any potential problems with &quot;use the lower of two&quot; in application are baked into the system. The previews contain an obvious mechanical counter-weight (Enhancements), potential counter-weights (Skill tricks), and explicit statements that powers will be designed to avoid potential disparities in dice pools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><b>That's what's pissing me off about your responses.</b></i> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> So what's pissing you off is that I can sit here and point out when you're wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm going to have to just disagree on this at principal, but you obviously feel that no one can have any opinion on not liking this initiative mechanic. So it doesn't matter to you. </div> </div> </div>What educational professional are you disagreeing with me on?<br /> <br /> Though more seriously, you haven't stated any principles that apply here, or made any case on why we should care about them.<br /> <br /> You are obviously only using the concept of principled positions to distract from not having a solid point, further demonstrated by resorting to ad hominems where you assign beliefs to me that have nothing to do with what I said.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with people not liking this initiative mechanic. Here's what I'm not fine with:<br /> <br /> 1) People making definitive judgements on an alpha slice document.<br /> <br /> 2) People declaring problems in the system that clearly don't exist.<br /> <br /> 3) People treating a mechanic that doesn't suit their personal preferences as the same thing as having actual mechanical problems.<br /> <br /> And whether or no something matters to me is hard to say if you haven't say what it is. You can't know if I care, or don't care, about a principle if you don't say what it is. But it makes a wonderful rhetorical device if we're not in text where I can sit here and think about it for more than a few seconds to see what you did there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even you noted that subtracting 1s heavily affected 'success' in cWoD, making players fail more. </div> </div> </div>No. I noted that it impacts success rates. Period. Stop there.<br /> <br /> Players don't &quot;fail more&quot; because there's nothing to fail more than. How often players fail isn't the issue in a vacuum. How often players fail compared to the expectations set by the system is where failing too much becomes an issue. The cWOD has a small issue with how it rates number of successes, but its very abstract and heavily ignored in mechanic heavy sections (like combat). The rates of success vs. fail/botch generally does match the expectations set in the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's incredibly dismissive. </div> </div> </div>No, it's confrontational because I'm frustrated that you're dodging questions. And you've apparently not moved on to labeling everything that's calling out the issues with your posts as &quot;dismissive.&quot; Which is still just a dodge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd want a system that actually let's people that roll higher go first. That's pretty simple. And doesn't require a tick wheel. </div> </div> </div>That's not a fix to a problem. That's a personal preference not being catered to and a house rule to address it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, I noted that if they made as dramatic a change to the background and setting <i><u>on top</u></i> of massive mechanics changes, they are setting themselves up to a similar situation that D&amp;D 4E and NuWoD ran into. </div> </div> </div>Which is going back to shifting goal posts. And there's this weird assumption that D&amp;D 4e and the nWOD are somehow in the same boat. D&amp;D 4e got canned after flopping. nWOD is about to get another crowdfunded prestige edition new game line, and is in the process of getting it's second edition updates out. WotC might consider D&amp;D 4e a failure from a business perspective, but OPP clearly doesn't consider the nWOD that.<br /> <br /> Yes, if the setting is drastically changed in Scion 2e, it risks alienating Scion 1e fans (though plenty of vocal fans on this forum have called for various setting changes; especially to be more true to the myths the game is based on). That's it. It could be a commercial flop (D&amp;D 4e), or be doing just fine from a business side of things (the nWOD). Alienated fans are always a risk with any changes; to the point that it's meaningless to get too worried about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they are specifically trying to do that, they shouldn't be trying to call is Scion 2E, they should be very upfront about calling it 'an entirely new game that shares some background assumptions about being a modern mythology.' Clear communication in that direction can stave off a lot of heartache and anger. </div> </div> </div>They haven't said this is their goal. So this whole line of debate is irrelevant. While it's been made clear there will be changes for Trinity and Scion in terms of setting, the developers have been pretty clear that the intention is it will still be fundamentally the core games that the 1e games were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T06:29:57-07:00","id":572593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://xkcd.com/386/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://imgs.xkcd.com/comics/duty_calls_2x.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://xkcd.com/386/\" target=\"_blank\"> Duty Calls </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://xkcd.com/386/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://xkcd.com/386/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Maybe just agree to disagree, and walk away? The devs have undoubtedly seen the pros and cons of both positions, and have weighted them appropriately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T21:18:41-07:00","id":573545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/561655-sardonyx-questions?p=572593#post572593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://xkcd.com/386/\" target=\"_blank\">https://xkcd.com/386/</a><br /> <br /> Maybe just agree to disagree, and walk away? The devs have undoubtedly seen the pros and cons of both positions, and have weighted them appropriately.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't hurting anything to discuss it, and if punches are thrown, we have mods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://rockpapercynic.com/index.php?date=2009-06-25\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.rockpapercynic.com/strips/2009-06-25.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rockpapercynic.com/index.php?date=2009-06-25\" target=\"_blank\"> Arguing on the Internet - a Rock Paper Cynic comic </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rockpapercynic.com/index.php?date=2009-06-25\" target=\"_blank\"> http://rockpapercynic.com/index.php?date=2009-06-25 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> in this comic, the Special Olympics are awesome so you shut your mouth </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","user":"Wolfgar","date":". 06-30-2015, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T22:22:28-07:00","id":573590,"title":"","content":"Heheheheh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}